# Test: RFC 7705 Section 4.2 -- ze opens with the globally configured AS first,
# and with the migration AS only after the peer answers Bad Peer AS.
# VALIDATES: RFC 7705 Section 4.2: "the speaker SHOULD send BGP OPEN using the
#            globally configured ASN first, and only send a BGP OPEN using the
#            locally configured ASN as a fallback if the remote neighbor responds
#            with the BGP error "Bad Peer AS"." Ze is AS 65000 with
#            `migration 65100`.
#              conn=1  ze's OPEN carries 65000 (0xFDE8) in My Autonomous System
#                      and in the Four-octet AS capability. The peer answers
#                      NOTIFICATION 2/2 Bad Peer AS.
#              conn=2  ze's next OPEN carries 65100 (0xFE4C) in both carriers.
#            Both carriers come from one resolution (openLocalAS,
#            session_as_migration.go), which is RFC7705-4.2-3 and AC-9's
#            agreement between header and capability.
# PREVENTS: a migrating speaker that keeps sending the refused AS, which is the
#           deadlock the SHOULD exists to avoid, and a header that names one AS
#           while the capability names the other.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: make noteASMigrationRejection (session_as_migration.go) return
# at once and conn=2's OPEN carries 65000 again, which the second expectation
# refuses.
#
# The OPEN frames are matched whole by inspect-open-message, so any capability
# ze adds changes them; only the two AS carriers are the subject here.

# ze-peer expectations
stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=tcp_connections:value=2
option=timeout:value=40s
option=open:value=inspect-open-message
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF002B0104FDE8005A0A0000020E020C01040001000141040000FDE8
action=send:conn=1:seq=2:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF0015030202
expect=bgp:conn=2:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF002B0104FE4C005A0A0000020E020C01040001000141040000FE4C
EOF_PEER

# ze bgp configuration
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65100
				migration 65100
			}
			router-id 10.0.0.2
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# Process orchestration
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=35s
